# Seamless Login via URL Payload

The goal is to provide a way to log a user in directly via a URL containing `UserName`, `Token`, and `timestamp`. We will create a **new Action method** to catch this payload, and we will extract the existing session generation code into a **new helper method** so both the existing [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) POST method and the new Action can share the exact same session setup logic.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Token Validation Strategy:** How should we validate the `Token` before generating the session? (e.g., checking a specific hash of `UserName + timestamp + secret`)?
> 2. **User Type (`UserType`):** What `UserType` should the seamless login default to (e.g., `"S"`)?

## Proposed Changes

### [LoginController.cs](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs)

#### [MODIFY] [LoginController.cs](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs)(file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs)

**1. Add a NEW `ActionResult` for Direct Login (`DirectLogin`)**
We will add a totally new GET method that accepts `UserName`, `Token`, and `timestamp`.

```csharp
[HttpGet]
[AllowAnonymous]
public ActionResult DirectLogin(string UserName, string Token, string timestamp)
{
    // 1. Validate the Timestamp and Token
    if (!IsValidPayload(UserName, Token, timestamp))
    {
        return RedirectToAction("Home", "Login", new { Error = PortalEncryption.EncryptPassword("Invalid login payload.") });
    }

    // 2. Mock a LoginRepository Modal
    LoginRepository Modal = new LoginRepository();
    Modal.UserName = UserName;
    Modal.UserType = "S"; 

    // 3. Authenticate User
    Modal = Modal.isValidUser(Modal);

    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Modal.Roles) && Modal.UserStatus != "Login Failed")
    {
        // 4. Reuse Session and Auth Cookie Generation logic
        CreateUserSession(Modal);

        return Redirect(Modal.UserTypeUrl);
    }
    else
    {
        return RedirectToAction("Home", "Login", new { Error = PortalEncryption.EncryptPassword("Direct login failed.") });
    }
}
```

**2. Extract Session Generation into a NEW method (`CreateUserSession`)**
We will create a new method `CreateUserSession(LoginRepository Modal)` that contains the cookie and session creation logic (lines 216-258 in [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) POST), and we'll update the [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) POST method to call this new helper method instead of duplicating the code.

